@startuml NeuralBrowser_DeploymentTopology
title NeuralBrowser — Physical Deployment Topology Diagram

skinparam {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #000000
  FontColor #000000
  FontName JetBrains Mono
  FontSize 12
  ArrowColor #000000
  ArrowThickness 1.2
  Shadowing false
  RoundCorner 0
  DefaultTextAlignment center
  Padding 8
  Margin 6
  LineThickness 1
  Monochrome true
  LineType ortho
}

skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #000000
  FontColor #000000
  BorderThickness 1.5
}

skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #000000
  FontColor #000000
  BorderThickness 1.2
}

node "Client Desktop PC" {
  node "Windows / Linux OS" {
    node "Python 3.11 Execution Environment" {
      artifact "NeuralBrowser Application (.py/.exe)" as App
      component "PyQt6 Engine" as PyQt
      component "QtWebEngine Core (Chromium)" as QWeb
    }

    node "Local LLM Daemon" {
      component "Ollama Service (localhost:11434)" as Ollama
      database "Local Weights Directory" {
        component "Phi-3 Mini Model" as Phi
        component "Llama-3 Model" as Llama
      }
    }

    database "Persistent User Storage" {
      file "config.json" as Conf
      file "bookmarks.json" as Book
      file "history.json" as Hist
    }
  }
}

node "Cloud Infrastructure" as Cloud {
  node "Groq API Server" {
    component "Groq Llama 3 Inference Engine" as GroqAPI
  }

  node "Gemini API Server" {
    component "Gemini Flash Inference Engine" as GemAPI
  }
}

App --> PyQt : <<binds>>
App --> QWeb : <<controls>>
App ..> Conf : <<reads/writes>>
App ..> Book : <<reads/writes>>
App ..> Hist : <<reads/writes>>

App --> Ollama : <<calls local API>>
Ollama --> Phi : <<loads>>
Ollama --> Llama : <<loads>>

App --> GroqAPI : <<calls model API>>
App --> GemAPI : <<calls model API>>

note top of App
  NeuralBrowser compiles all dependencies 
  locally. Performs zero tracking or cloud telemetry, 
  saving bookmarks and histories in pure local files.
end note

note right of Ollama
  Autonomous ReAct Agent utilizes local Ollama 
  to run operations. Keeps all webpage scanning 
  and processing data locally on client machine.
end note

@enduml
